 MANY model. Both will be cognizant of the JOIN model, however. This is a rare scenario. Let\u2019s use a bizarre, somewhat contrived, and controversial example. Let\u2019s say we have a ONE side model, God. The MANY side model would be Human. Each God could have MANY Humans following him/her through a JOIN model of GuardianAngel. The God model could have many GuardianAngels but lets say s/he doesn\u2019t care about keeping track of all his/her follower Humans. Who said DB associations were boring?","topics":[],"score":184384,"global_rank":391086},{"name":"CrossTheStreams/rails_3_boilerplate","owner":"CrossTheStreams","html_url":"https://github.com/CrossTheStreams/rails_3_boilerplate","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184384,"global_rank":391087},{"name":"MargeRosen/horoscope","owner":"MargeRosen","html_url":"https://github.com/MargeRosen/horoscope","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184384,"global_rank":391088},{"name":"bvuongx/Recipes_you_name_it","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/Recipes_you_name_it","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184384,"global_rank":391090},{"name":"bvuongx/Recipes","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/Recipes","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":184384,"global_rank":391091},{"name":"justinfaulkner/mog_simulator","owner":"justinfaulkner","html_url":"https://github.com/justinfaulkner/mog_simulator","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":"A simulator for a board game I'm designing called Ministry of Green","topics":[],"score":184382,"global_rank":391099},{"name":"ColetteIsabella/Beewatcher","owner":"ColetteIsabella","html_url":"https://github.com/ColetteIsabella/Beewatcher","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":